{
  "sn48.57:0.1": "Linked Discourses 48.57 ",
  "sn48.57:0.2": "6. The Boar’s Cave ",
  "sn48.57:0.3": "With the Divinity Sahampati ",
  "sn48.57:1.1": "At one time, when he was first awakened, the Buddha was staying in Uruvelā at the goatherd’s banyan tree on the bank of the Nerañjarā River. ",
  "sn48.57:1.2": "Then as he was in private retreat this thought came to his mind, ",
  "sn48.57:1.3": "“When these five faculties are developed and cultivated they have freedom from death as their objective, destination, and culmination. ",
  "sn48.57:1.4": "What five? ",
  "sn48.57:1.5": "The faculties of faith, ",
  "sn48.57:1.6": "energy, ",
  "sn48.57:1.7": "mindfulness, ",
  "sn48.57:1.8": "immersion, ",
  "sn48.57:1.9": "and wisdom. ",
  "sn48.57:1.10": "When these five faculties are developed and cultivated they have freedom from death as their objective, destination, and culmination.” ",
  "sn48.57:2.1": "Then the divinity Sahampati knew the Buddha’s train of thought. As easily as a strong person would extend or contract their arm, he vanished from the realm of divinity and reappeared in front of the Buddha. ",
  "sn48.57:2.2": "He arranged his robe over one shoulder, raised his cupped palms toward the Buddha, and said: ",
  "sn48.57:2.3": "“That’s so true, Blessed One! That’s so true, Holy One! ",
  "sn48.57:2.4": "When these five faculties are developed and cultivated they have freedom from death as their objective, destination, and culmination. ",
  "sn48.57:2.5": "What five? ",
  "sn48.5